+  # rather than deleting the whole line — the stub libpng.pc's Requires may
+  # legitimately list other real deps (e.g. libpng16) alongside zlib on the
+  # same line, so blindly deleting the line would break that too. pkg-config
+  # accepts either comma- or space-separated Requires lists, so normalizing
+  # commas to spaces after stripping the token is safe and avoids dangling
+  # punctuation (e.g. "libpng16, zlib" -> "libpng16 ,      -> normalize ->
+  # "libpng16").
